C3 — single-account series: no drift.  MET, by exhaustive differential test.
A generated matrix of 82,320 single-account scenarios (7 frequencies incl.
invalid/empty x 5 amounts x 7 anchor balances incl. negative/zero x 4
thresholds x 7 NextExpected dates straddling the 35-day horizon edges x 4
single-account legsets x 3 asOf dates), dumping Available/Minimum/Crossing/
SuggestedTopUp/Threshold/err for each, run against BOTH trees:
  $ cd <scratch>/b2old  && DUMP_OUT=dump_old.txt go test -run TestDump_SingleAccountMatrix ...  -> wrote 82320 rows
  $ cd <scratch>/b2copy && DUMP_OUT=dump_new.txt go test -run TestDump_SingleAccountMatrix ...  -> wrote 82320 rows
  $ diff dump_old.txt dump_new.txt
    NO DIFFERENCES
Byte-identical output pre- and post-change over the whole matrix.
The worker's TestProject_SingleAccountSeriesUnaffected also passes against the
pre-change tree, which is the correct behaviour for a no-drift guard.

